    "attributes": {
      "usb": "USB Type-C",
      "connection": "40 unpopulated pads + battery/solar/GNSS + 2 U.FL",
      "interface": "USB / GPIO / SPI",
      "chip": "ESP32-S3R2 + SX1262"
    },
    "scope": "V4.3.1 mechanical reference, OLED and protective PC frame fitted, no installed header pins. Manufacturer envelope 51.69 \u00d7 25.40 \u00d7 10.70 mm without pins (15.60 mm with pins). Frame 33.00 \u00d7 18.60 mm, display aperture 22.00 \u00d7 11.40 mm follow the page 15 drawing. Four PCB bores are 2.80 mm in the official V4.3.1 STEP; the datasheet labels 1.90 mm in the protective-frame fastener area. PCB thickness, outline transitions, individual component geometry/positions, display recess and USB overhang are approximate. Includes battery, solar and GNSS connector envelopes plus two U.FL sockets; no V3 spring antenna. External antenna, flexible leads, battery, mating connectors and loose headers are excluded. RF hardware revisions and R8 electrical variants must be checked against the ordered board. The OLED glass, active face and guard aperture are centered at local X=+2.00 mm, Y=-6.35 mm following the user-requested handheld display fit correction; the outer protective frame and PCB remain centered at X=0. These display datums include the user-requested 2 mm left and 1 mm upward fit corrections and are a user fit calibration, not a newly verified manufacturer dimension.",
    "references": [
      "https://heltec.org/project/wifi-lora-32-v4/",
      "https://wiki.heltec.org/docs/devices/open-source-hardware/esp32-series/lora-32/wifi-lora-32-v4/",
